---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import PlaceholderPage from '../components/PlaceholderPage.astro'
import { company, contact } from '../data/site'

// TODO: check this draft before launch, especially how long enquiries are kept
const updated = '4 November 2026'
const h2 = 'pt-6 text-2xl leading-tight font-heavy text-coral-ink xl:text-d31'
const link = 'underline underline-offset-4'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy | Bit More Media"
  description="How Bit More Media uses the information you give us when you get in touch."
>
  <PlaceholderPage title="Privacy policy">
    <p>Last updated {updated}.</p>
    <p>
      This policy explains what information we collect when you use this website or get in touch,
      what we do with it and the rights you have.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This website is run by {company.name}, a company registered in England and Wales (company
      number {company.number}), registered office {company.registeredOffice}. We’re responsible for
      your personal information under UK data protection law (UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act
      2018). Questions about this policy? Email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`} class={link}>
        {contact.email}
      </a>
      .
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      <strong class="font-heavy">When you email or call us:</strong> whatever details you choose to
      share, such as your name, email address, phone number and what you’d like to talk about.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong class="font-heavy">When you visit the site:</strong> like most websites, our hosting
      server keeps standard technical logs (such as your IP address, browser type and the pages
      requested) to keep the site secure and working.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Cookies and tracking</h2>
    <p>
      This website doesn’t use cookies, analytics or advertising trackers. Our fonts and images are
      served from our own server, so visiting the site doesn’t send your details to anyone else.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>How we use your information</h2>
    <p>
      We use the details you send us to reply to your enquiry and, if you become a client, to
      provide our services. We don’t use them for marketing, we don’t sell them and we don’t share
      them with anyone else except the service providers below.
    </p>
    <p>
      Our lawful basis is our legitimate interest in replying to people who get in touch with us. If
      we go on to work together, we’ll use your details as needed to carry out our contract with
      you.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Who else handles your information</h2>
    <p>
      <strong class="font-heavy">Kualo</strong> hosts this website in the UK.{' '}
      <strong class="font-heavy">Google</strong> (Google Workspace) provides our email, so your
      enquiry is stored in our inbox. Google may store data outside the UK, protected by the
      safeguards UK law requires. Both act only on our instructions.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      If your enquiry doesn’t lead to any work, we delete it within two years. If you become a
      client, we keep your details for as long as we work together, and then for as long as the law
      requires us to keep business records (usually six years).
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us to give you a copy of your information, correct it, delete it or stop using it.
      Just email{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`} class={link}>
        {contact.email}
      </a>{' '}
      and we’ll reply within one month.
    </p>
    <p>
      If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your information, please tell us first so we can put
      it right. You also have the right to complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office (ICO)
      at{' '}
      <a href="https://ico.org.uk/make-a-complaint/" class={link}>
        ico.org.uk
      </a>{' '}
      or on 0303 123 1113.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy, we’ll update it here and change the date at the top.</p>
  </PlaceholderPage>
</BaseLayout>
